\f0\fs22 \cf0 My font 
\f1\i Solough
\f0\i0  was inspired by two things that bring me happiness: sunlight and the lakes of Cavan. While observing the lake on a sunny weekend, I noticed the refraction of light creating patterns on the lake bed. \
\
Looking closer at these patterns I started to make out different shapes, which eventually formed letters. This was my main inspiration for this font.\
\
After creating my font, I wanted to further capture its organic and flowy nature by complementing it with a fold-out book. As the reader unravels the book, a pop up map is revealed, camouflaged within the patterns. \
\
This map showcases how the font could be used within poster format. It displays the lake that inspired me to create this font: Lough Ramor. I printed the type specimen in Riso Blue, tying the theme back to its watery origins.}